course: dictionary
lesson: 6142
title: Context clues with a plant
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Context means the words and sentences around a word. When you meet a new word, look at the words near it for clues. «Monarchs taste bad to birds because their caterpillars eat poisonous milkweed.» The word poisonous is a big clue. A plant that is poisonous can harm whatever eats it, so milkweed must be a plant.
explain: Milkweed is a noun, so it names a thing. Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Monarch caterpillars eat milkweed» still makes sense if you read it as «Monarch caterpillars eat a plant», so your meaning fits.
explain: Look at the phrases too. «Milkweed pods» and «plant milkweed» show you how the word is used. In a sentence, the pods are part of the plant, so you can guess they are part of it, not a separate thing. A dictionary confirms it: the pods are full of fluffy seeds.
fact: Milkweed is a North American plant, which means it grows in North America.
fact: Milkweed has a milky white sap, pinkish flower clusters and pods full of fluffy seeds.
fact: Milkweed is the only food monarch butterfly caterpillars eat.
fact: The plant's poison makes monarch caterpillars taste bad to birds.
fact: Schools in the USA and Canada plant milkweed gardens to help monarchs.
exercise: «Monarch caterpillars eat milkweed, and birds that eat a monarch get sick.» What is milkweed? | A type of butterfly with orange and black wings | *A North American plant with milky white sap and fluffy seeds | A sweet fruit grown in gardens | A kind of bird that eats butterflies
exercise: «Monarchs taste bad to birds because their caterpillars eat poisonous milkweed.» Find and copy the one word that tells you the plant is harmful. | *poisonous | birds | monarchs | caterpillars
exercise: Why do monarch caterpillars need milkweed? | They like the taste of its pods | *It is the only food they eat | It keeps birds away from the sun | They sleep in its flowers all winter
test: «The Camel came by "chewing milkweed most 'scruciating idle"» What is the Camel doing with the milkweed? | Planting it | Selling it | *Chewing it | Painting it
test: What does «milkweed pods» mean? | Bird nests made from milk | Butterflies that glow in the dark | Small bags of sugar | *The seed cases of the plant, full of fluffy seeds
exam: A school plants a milkweed garden to help monarchs. What is the best reason, using what you have learned? | Milkweed grows only in snow | *Monarch caterpillars need its leaves to eat | Birds need milkweed to fly | Milkweed is a kind of bee
